## Citation Rules
- Always use [@key] Pandoc syntax in .qmd files
- cite-method: natbib is set in all chapter YAML
- PDF output: Quarto auto-converts [@key] → \citep{key} via natbib
- Docx output: citeproc uses per-chapter CSL files
  - templates/csl/ama.csl  → CH_2, CH_3, CH_4, CH_6 (AMA numbered)
  - templates/csl/mdpi.csl → CH_1, CH_5 (MDPI numbered)

## Template Rules
- MDPI (CH_1, CH_5): format block is `pdf:` with `template:` override
- Wiley (CH_2, CH_3, CH_4): format block is `wiley-njd-pdf:` with `template:` override
- build.ps1 uses `--to pdf` for MDPI, `--to wiley-njd-pdf` for Wiley
- Never switch these — using `--to pdf` on a Wiley chapter renders without the journal template
- WileyNJDv5 class only (WileyNJD-v2 is deprecated)
- Wiley extension: _extensions/ramiromagno/wiley-njd/

## YAML Reserved Fields (renamed in CH_1/CH_5 to avoid Quarto conflicts)
- journal:       → target-journal:
- abbreviations: → manuscript-abbreviations:
- articletype:   → target-articletype:
- biblio-style:  REMOVED (mdpi.cls sets it internally)

## LaTeX Shims (already in templates — do not remove)
- \providecommand{\tightlist}{} — all templates
- \let\listoflistings\relax — all templates
- \usepackage{calc} — for \real{} in Pandoc longtable column widths
- longtable 2-column patch — cpt_psp_template.tex only (STIX2COL is 2-column)

## Inline Math Rule
- NEVER write $\cmd$digit — Quarto drops the math when a digit immediately follows $
- Correct: ${\sim}1.2$ M   Wrong: $\sim$1.2 M

